I have a 667 MHz XP900/DS10 alphaserver running Tru64 5.1B that 
currently has three internal ultra-2 SCSI disks (two 9.1 GB and 
one 18.2 GB) attached to a KZPCA-AX PCI SCSI adapter card. 
This setup works fine. However, I need more disk space, so I want 
to replace one (or perhaps both) of the 9.1GB drives with larger 
drives.  My questions are:

- what's the max single disk size that the KZPCA-AX controller can handle?
  Can it take 36.4GB disks ?
- what is the maximum total internal disk capacity on this system ?
- any suggestions for which HP/Compaq part numbers to look for ?

I also have a second PCI SCSI adapter card (KZPBA-CX) spare that 
I could add in to the system, if that would help.
(BTW my understanding is that the KZPCA-AX and KZPCA-AA adapters 
are essentially the same, being a Symbios SYM8952U). 

Thanks for any suggestions.

Martin

