Hello,
My Original Question,

Tru64 4.0G AlphaServer 2000 and I have ran into problems

Last week we had power go down in the computer room. When power was restored I 
noticed that I had a hard drive go down. It had a fault light on it. Member 1 
on a raid-5 4 member set.

I put in my spare drive and the system auto rebuilt the drive.
Since it was under contract I got another drive to replace my spare.

On Sunday we had another power outage (the UPS is old 1/2 size of the computer 
room) and I had a failed drive again. Same member, same raid set, same 
rebuild.

Is there anything else I need to check to see why this keeps on happening?

The only Response I received was from kazuro.furukawa@kek.jp  who said it 
might be a heat issue.

I talked to HP tech and he said don't worry about it to much because of the 
age of the drives etc.
